==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*snutraz}}, perhaps from the same Indo-European root as Greek [[νοος]] ‘mind’. Cognate with Old High German [[snottar]], Old Norse [[snotr]], Gothic [[𐍃𐌽𐌿𐍄𐍂𐍃]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsnotor/|lang=ang}}

